WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.164
G P S and other global navigation satellite systems support drone position, navigation,

00:00:06.164 --> 00:00:08.963
automation, return-to-home, logs, metadata, and timing.

00:00:08.963 --> 00:00:13.162
These conveniences create operational dependencies that must be understood.

00:00:13.162 --> 00:00:15.494
Jamming degrades or blocks reception.

00:00:15.494 --> 00:00:19.692
Spoofing attempts to mislead a receiver with deceptive information.

00:00:19.692 --> 00:00:23.424
Weak lock, drift, warnings, cue disagreement, impossible movement,

00:00:23.424 --> 00:00:27.156
or unexpected routing are indicators, not automatic proof.

00:00:27.156 --> 00:00:30.888
Environmental obstruction, reflected signals, compass interference, antenna problems,

00:00:30.888 --> 00:00:35.086
receiver faults, and software issues can produce similar symptoms.

00:00:35.086 --> 00:00:40.684
Compare map, visual, compass, telemetry, mode, and site context while preserving uncertainty.

00:00:40.684 --> 00:00:44.883
Plan defensively with preflight checks, visual references, manual-control readiness,

00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:50.014
conservative automation, abort criteria, emergency landing areas, and documented crew roles.

00:00:50.014 --> 00:00:54.212
When navigation is unreliable, protect people and recover early.

00:00:54.212 --> 00:00:57.011
Never transmit interfering or deceptive signals.

00:00:57.011 --> 00:01:02.143
Preserve logs and evidence, report through appropriate safety and regulatory channels,

00:01:02.143 --> 00:01:04.009
and coordinate qualified review.

00:01:04.009 --> 00:01:09.140
The goal is resilience and safe decision-making, not experimentation with interference.
